{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122604","id":4315960766,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAUBVvg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122604","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122604.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122604.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122604","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122604/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122604/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122604/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/64489caeddb36c3a92158d8740ead0c95bd49a3b","number":122604,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix grid snapping overriding surface placement height","user":{"login":"Bat-Computer","id":40317509,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzE3NTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40317509?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer","html_url":"https://github.com/Bat-Computer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bat-Computer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen grid snapping is enabled, dragging a 3D scene onto a surface with collision can cause the placed object to sink into or float above the surface.\r\n\r\nThe collision-aware placement calculation correctly determines the surface contact position, but `snap_point()` subsequently snaps all three axes, including the vertical axis. This overwrites the precise surface-contact height.\r\n\r\nThis PR preserves the Y coordinate calculated by `_get_instance_position()` while still applying grid snapping to the horizontal axes.\r\n\r\nThe same issue also affects collision repositioning of an existing selected node, so the same behaviour is applied there for consistency.\r\n\r\n- Closes #122552\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nTested in a Windows developer build.\r\n\r\nTested with:\r\n- Dragging 3D scenes onto flat collision surfaces.\r\n- Dragging onto surfaces at different heights.\r\n- Dragging onto sloped collision surfaces.\r\n- Grid snapping enabled.\r\n- Collision repositioning of existing nodes.\r\n- Placement through an editor plugin using the standard 3D viewport drag-and-drop behaviour.\r\n\r\nObjects retain their upright orientation when placed on slopes, as expected, while their lowest bounds remain correctly positioned against the collision surface.\r\n\r\nI used AI to help finding the issue, source-code navigation, discussion of the proposed fix, and preparation of the pull request. I have manually reviewed the source changes, compiled the modified engine, and tested the resulting build.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-19T17:12:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T18:30:36Z","closed_at":"2026-08-19T18:04:17Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f80e452539eec6bad2e